 ideal $\\mathfrak m$ the ring $R_{\\mathfrak m}$\nis a normal domain."], "source_environment": "lemma", "source_environment_end_line": 8186, "source_environment_start_line": 8176, "source_filename": "algebra.tex", "source_has_equivalence_form": true, "source_has_multi_part_form": true, "source_label": "lemma-normality-is-local", "source_lemma_local_hypotheses_persist_after_end": false, "source_pass1_pass2_unchanged": true, "source_pass2_context_status": "resolved", "source_ref_semantic_expansion_final_approved": false, "source_refs": [], "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_statement_line": 8176, "source_url": "https://github.com/stacks/stacks-project/blob/a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14/algebra.tex#L8176", "standalone_statement_tex": "Let $R$ be a domain. The following are equivalent:\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item The domain $R$ is a normal domain,\n\\item for every prime $\\mathfrak p \\subset R$ the local ring\n$R_{\\mathfrak p}$ is a normal domain, and\n\\item for every maximal ideal $\\mathfrak m$ the ring $R_{\\mathfrak m}$\nis a normal domain.\n\\end{enumerate}", "status": "standalone_draft_ready_for_validation", "unconditional_section_hypotheses": []}
